'Harassment', 'x-ONLY groups', 'gender verification issues' ....

All I hear in this thread is a re-statement of the 'Yugoslavian
Syndrome'. 

"These people are not quite like us, and this bothers us" - so the
obvious solution is to segregate 'us' from 'them'. Once you begin
such an excercise, history reveals its ultimate outcome again and
again - slavery or genocide.

How is a 'women only' group any different in principal from a 
country club that excludes Jews ? How is this 'gender verification'
issue any different in principle  from the NAZIs insistance that
Germans be able to prove their bloodline was 'pure' of semetic
'corruption' ? Why is the effort to censor annoying persons or
data any different in principle from 'ethnic cleansing' ?

Attempting to minimize personal annoyance through institutional
authority, through segregation, through ideological litmus tests,
through censorship, these things are the very seeds from which
our most vile collective evils have emerged. 

EVERYONE is the recipient of some form of harassment during an
average day. Some harassment is institutional, some cultural, 
some personal, some simply the result of circumstances. Women
have no special claims as to quality or quantity insofar as
'harassment' is concerned. To seriously attempt to alter
the entire world and the thinking of everyone in it simply
to ease ones minor peeves is remnicient of a child throwing
a temper tantrum because they wanted the  blue horsie toy
rather than the yellow one. Translating such egocentric
impulses into the adult world is positively dangerous - and
has been proven so more often than we like to admit.

To whomever --- shut up and take your daily lumps like the
rest of us. Act like an adult, not like a spoiled child.
You can't have everything just the way you want it - and
neither can anyone else. Lastly, if you expect me to spend
my hard-earned tax money on universities which permit, condone
and codify these primitive manifestations of racism - FORGET IT !

-- Jim Mason 


