----------------------------------------------------------------------
                                                               11-DEC-1992



RULES FOR USE OF COMPUTER SYSTEMS AND THE COMPUTER NETWORK


              Approved in the board of the ADP center and the
	      ADP office of physics on 11 December 1992



I   INTRODUCTION

      1.      The purpose of the University of Helsinki is to offer persons
	      working in connection with the University good possibilities
	      for the use of computers and telecommunications.  To
	      guarantee good working conditions, the following jointly
 	      agreed-to rules need to be conformed to.  The purpose of the
	      rules is to define the rights and duties of the users
	      and administrators of the system.

      2.      These rules will be applied in all computer systems and networks
	      governed by the ADP center or the physics ADP office,
	      and the parts relevant to users will also be applied
	      to other systems whenever the account or possibility
	      to use is received via the ADP center or the physics
	      ADP office.  In the rest of the document, the ADP center
	      and physics ADP office will be known as administrators
	      of the systems.

      3.      Corresponding rules about acceptable use and ethics of use
	      are in force in many other communities, of which the University
	      computing systems can be interpreted to be part of, or to which
	      there are connections from the University computing systems.
	      Some examples of these communities are FUNET, Nordunet and
	      NSFnet (of United States of America).

      4.      The rules are based on the following generic principles:

              - Everyone has a possibility for proper use.

              - It is not allowed to cause trouble to others.

              - Privacy shall be honored.


       5.     The administrators can give complementary instructions
	      to these rules concerning the use of separate equipment,
	      software and networks.  Examples of these are:

                        -   instructions concerning conferencing systems
                        -   instructions for use of microcomputer rooms
			    ("ADP stations")
                        -   instructions for use of passwords



II   DUTIES OF ADMINISTRATORS


      1.      Administrators take care of maintaining good working conditions.
	      Named people have responsibilities for the implementation
	      of the maintenance of the computing and telecommunications
	      systems in practice.

      2.      Accounts in generic machines will be given by application
	      to university employees, and to students who need it in their
	      studies.  The application is to be given to the ADP contact
	      person.

      3.      The basic instructions concerning the use of the systems
	      are available at the customer service of the ADP center
	      and the physics ADP office.  The instructions are also
	      readable in the University electronic information system
	      (HELI).  Administrators will publicize changes made in the
	      system and the effects thereof, and provide guidance when
	      needed.

      4.      The administration personnel has a duty to keep matters
	      confidential ("a duty to keep things secret", a phrase
	      used for example with doctors, lawyers and the like //jkp).



III   RIGHTS OF ADMINISTRATORS

      1.      To fulfill their duties, the administrative personnel
	      has permission to restrict and control use of the
	      systems.

      2.      Named people responsible for each system have a right
	      to read files of users, if urgent investigation of the
	      system's state in a disorder situation that demands,
	      or misuse of the systems is suspected.



IV    DUTIES OF USERS

      1.      To make good working conditions possible, each user shall
	      be responsible in the use of the systems.  These instructions
	      govern systems, whose use demands logging in (multi-user
	      machines or workstations) and for the applicable parts
	      equipment, whose use does not demand user recognition
	      (microcomputers and data communications equipment).

      2.      Each person must always use their own name and user id
	      except in the cases where anonymous or pseudonymous
	      usage is explicitly allowed.  An exception is also
	      use of course and group accounts given for a specific
	      purpose.  The account holder is responsible that the use
	      of the account is in accordance with the account
	      application.

      3.      Users must consider the other users of the system.

      4.      Users must take care of issues connected to common
	      computer security.  Even if the user herself doesn't
	      have anything particular to protect, others may have.
	      Proper handling of the password is necessary to
	      prevent misuse.  All users have the responsibility
	      for the total security of the system.

      5.      Instructions given must be followed (see II 3.).



V    RIGHTS OF USERS

      1.      Account holders have a right to use the equipment and the
	      computer network in ways they need, as long as usage is connected
	      with University activities, which is interpreted to mean
	      research, studying, teaching and management.

      2.      Users can make initiatives to the administrators, concerning
	      development of ADP services.

      3.      An user can make an individualized complaint to the director
	      or board of the ADP center or the physics ADP office in case
	      she is not satisfied with the actions directed at her by
	      the administration personnel.



VI   RESTRICTIONS ON USE


      1.      Disturbing other users is forbidden.  Forbidden are
	      both direct disturbance and indirect, for example one
	      resulting from waste of computer or network resources.

      2.      Use of University computer equipment, computer network
	      and communications resources must have connection to
	      research, teaching, studying or management and the
	      resources must be used in accordance with the conditions
	      of the account.  Using a no-payment account for business
	      or profit use is strictly forbidden.  For-pay usage
	      shall be separately negotiated.

      3.      Using systems which demand a personal account is forbidden,
	      if no current personal account exists.  Attempting to
	      get into the system with a wrong account and exceeding
	      the powers of one's own id or attempting such are forbidden.
	      Usage of equipment or the network to try to break into
	      other systems is forbidden.

      4.      Modifications to equipment or system software are forbidden.
	      This holds also for single-user systems in public use.

      5.      Getting around quotas and other limits on use, or attempting
	      such, is forbidden.

      6.      Search for or using known or new security holes is forbidden.

      7.      Copying of programs, software or files without permission is
	      forbidden.



VII   MISUSE AND CONSEQUENCES THEREOF

      1.      Misuse of computer or telecommunications equipment means
	      all action, which

                       -    disturbs use of the system for the purpose
	   		    it has primarily been set up for

                       -    causes disturbances in the computer network
			    to which the system is connected to, or in
			    another system in the network

                       -    is in violation of given rules

                       -    uses such parts of features of the system
		            whose use is forbidden in instructions

                       -    has been prohibited by the responsible person
			    or owner of the system

       2.     In the University environment, in misuse cases concerning
	      computing and telecommunications systems, primarily
	      University's own investagative and restrictive acts will
	      be used.  On suspicions of misuse, the following procedure
	      will be followed:

                       -    The administrator of the system or the ADP
		   	    contact person of the faculty in question
			    will contact the user and clarify what
			    the act is about and announce her own stand
			    with regard to continuing the action.

                       -    Depending on the nature of the misuse,
			    a warning can be given to the user,
			    or limitations concerning use can be given,
			    or use can be forbidden for a fixed time.

                       -    Warning or a limitation on use can be given
			    by the director of the ADP center or the physics
			    ADP office, section chief or the ADP contact
			    person of a faculty.

                       -    Fixed time prohibition on use can be given
			    by the director of the ADP center or the physics
			    ADP office.  Prohibition on use can be given
			    on University internal misuse and when the action
		    	    continues despite a warning.

                       -    Named persons responsible for systems have, if they
			    so deem necessary ("unavoidable"), to restrict or
			    hinder use of systems for the time the
			    investigation is ongoing.

                       -    In investigating the matter, the user and other
			    parties concerned shall be heard.  As a result
			    of the investigation, it will be determined
		  	    what actions will be taken.  The user has a right
			    to appeal to the board about the decision.

       3.     The user must take into consideration that the personal
	      data protection act, criminal code and copyright law
	      have rules regulating use of ADP.

       4.     If misuse is serious or the target has been outside
	      the University and the act is criminal, University
	      can give the matter to police to investigate.
